+# Round 8 T-dense research report
+
+HEURISTIC status: work in progress. Only this report and tdense8_scratch are being edited; no commits or subagents. Mathematical computation is restricted to `DIRICHLET_IP=34.148.157.169 src/dirun.sh -c 2`. Optimization uses Gurobi with two threads and NonConvex=2 where applicable. No kernel verification or external priority is asserted.
+
+PROVED target (quoted): T-dense(C) means that there exists c(C)>0 such that every nonempty finite set A of distinct positive integers with X=max A<=C|A| satisfies M(A)>=c(C)sqrt(|A|), for f_A(x)=sum cos(ax) and M=-min over the entire circle.
+
+PROVED source audit: read CLAUDE.md, the complete round-8 brief, P17, P31/P31-N/P31-E, P32, P40, P47, P48, P52/P53, P54/P55, P58, NOTEBOOK continuations 9–10, E16/E78, and the round-7 report and exact witness code. P17(a), P58's high-pass diagonal and its assembly are quoted inputs, not round-8 discoveries. A grep of PROOFS.md for the improved constant and separable/doubling-potential method found no corresponding entry. This is an internal novelty check, not an external priority claim.
+
+## Task 1: rigorous doubly-positive bound
+
+PROVED (paper argument, newly derived relative to the inspected record). Let w be any nonzero continuous even integrable nonnegative positive-definite function on R. Normalize w(0)=1 and put s=1/sqrt(2), b=1-s. Then
+
+    w(t)^2 <= s w(t) + b w(2t)    for every real t.
+
+Indeed write x=w(t), y=w(2t). Positive definiteness gives 0<=x,y<=1 and y>=2x^2-1. For x<=s use x^2<=s x. For s<=x<=1, subtract the right-hand side with y replaced by 2x^2-1: the result is
+
+    (2s-1)(x-s)(x-1) <= 0.
+
+Integrating and changing variables in the dilation term gives
+
+    integral w^2 <= ((1+s)/2) integral w,
+    rho* <= (2+sqrt(2))/4 = 0.8535533906... .
+
+PROVED this improves quoted P17(a)'s 0.90565 for its full class, not just autocorrelations. P58 therefore proves T-dense(C) for every C<(2/r)(1+sqrt(1-(2+sqrt(2))/4))^2, with r the quoted asymptotic P31 constant. Exact numerical reach and a possible polynomial-potential refinement are being checked on the VM.
+
+HEURISTIC bounded follow-up: use a monotone polynomial beta and certify
+
+    rho x-x^2+beta(max(0,2x^2-1))-beta(x)/2 >= 0,
+
+which integrates to the desired gap. Sampling may discover beta; only exact rational polynomial inequalities will support a theorem. General doubly-positive numerical optimization will be compared with the autocorrelation subclass at the same resolution.
+
+## Task 2: two-scale programme
+
+HEURISTIC active lines: (i) local window constraints at individual mesoscopic spikes, retaining the distinction between amplitude and energy; (ii) aggregated filtered spike measures and higher/product windows; (iii) a phase-consistent binary realization test for any surviving formal escape. The round-7 witness is the common adversarial input. No escape or extension beyond C=6.054 has yet been established in this round.
+
+## Task 3
+
+HEURISTIC deferred until Tasks 1 and 2 have substantive outcomes, as instructed.

